<article class="env-lemma" id="0F3U">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F3U">Lemma <span data-tag="0F3U">38.33.1</span>.</a> Let $X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. If $X = U \cup V$ is an open cover such that $U \to S$ and $V \to S$ are separated and $U \cap V \to U \times _ S V$ is closed, then $X \to S$ is separated. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. Hint: check that $\Delta : X \to X \times _ S X$ is closed by using the open covering of $X \times _ S X$ given by $U \times _ S U$, $U \times _ S V$, $V \times _ S U$, and $V \times _ S V$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>